      "id": 1,
      "text": "Hamilton began in 1795 as Payne’s Settlement, a modest crossroads named after early settler Elisha Payne.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4,
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.thisishamiltonny.com/abouthamilton",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "State Route 12B runs along Hamilton’s western edge, linking the village north to Madison and south to Earlville.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        15
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hamilton%2C_New_York",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Hamilton sits within the Chenango River watershed, where the river briefly enters the town near its southwest corner.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        16
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hamilton%2C_New_York",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "route_only"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Sangerfield River cuts across Hamilton from northeast to southwest, joining the Chenango south of Earlville.",
